  "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $10$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.6x & =-3.6 \\\\ 10\\cdot (0.6x) & =10\\cdot (-3.6) \\\\ 6x & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the equation using the multiplication principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & =-36 \\\\ \\frac{6x}{6} & =\\frac{-36}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{6}x}{\\cancel{6}} & =\\frac{-36}{6} \\\\ x & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
